---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="LDiHK | Social Media Analytics for Preventive Mental Health">
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white py-24 lg:py-32">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#F4F0E4_1px,transparent_1px),linear-gradient(to_bottom,#F4F0E4_1px,transparent_1px)] bg-[size:4rem_4rem] [mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_50%_at_50%_0%,#000_70%,transparent_100%)] opacity-60"></div>

    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center space-y-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-teal/10 border border-brand-teal/20 text-xs font-bold text-brand-teal tracking-wide uppercase">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-teal animate-pulse"></span>
          InsurTech for Preventive Mental Health
        </div>
        <a href="#hackathon" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-peach/10 border border-brand-peach/30 text-xs font-bold text-brand-navy tracking-wide uppercase hover:bg-brand-peach/20 transition-colors">
          Hackathon Project &middot; Munich 2026
        </a>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight max-w-4xl mx-auto leading-[1.15] text-left sm:text-center">
        Your Social Media Footprint as an <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-teal via-brand-navy to-brand-peach">Early Signal</span> for Mental Health
      </h1>

      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-brand-navy/70 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed text-left sm:text-center">
        LDiHK turns the data exports every user can request under privacy law (YouTube via Google Takeout, Instagram and TikTok) into an anonymous picture of their digital habits: how much, how fragmented and how late at night they use social media. Our concept: together with insurers, build models that recognise depression risk early, so prevention can start before treatment becomes necessary, rewarding healthier habits along the way.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 pt-4">
        <a
          href="/dashboard"
          class="w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-teal text-white font-bold text-base hover:bg-brand-teal/95 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-brand-teal/20 hover:shadow-xl hover:-translate-y-0.5 active:translate-y-0 duration-150 flex items-center justify-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"
          id="hero-cta-dashboard"
        >
          Try the Console with Your Data
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6" />
          </svg>
        </a>
        <a
          href="#science"
          class="w-full sm:w-auto px-8 py-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-beige text-brand-navy font-bold text-base hover:bg-brand-navy/10 transition-all border border-brand-navy/20 duration-150 flex items-center justify-center cursor-pointer"
          id="hero-cta-how-it-works"
        >
          How It Works
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Project origin -->
  <section id="hackathon" class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-brand-navy/5 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-brand-navy/10 bg-brand-beige/30 p-6 sm:p-10 space-y-4">
        <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-md bg-brand-peach/20 text-brand-navy font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
          About this project
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
          Built at the EuroTech x Hong Kong Talent Exchange Hackathon 2026 in Munich
        </h2>
        <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          LDiHK (Life Data Intelligence Hong Kong) was created by a team of four for the EuroTech x HKTE Hackathon 2026.
          The challenge we chose: Hong Kong's mental health care is overloaded, with long waits for psychiatric referrals,
          while decades of research link heavy, fragmented and late-night social media use to depression risk.
        </p>
        <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          This website is the working prototype from the hackathon. You can upload your own data exports and see your usage
          patterns, a comparison with a synthetic population and a study-based risk indicator. The insurance partnerships,
          roadmap and business model below are the concept we pitched to the jury. No insurer is involved, and no data is
          shared with anyone.
        </p>
        <a href="https://marlonmueller.eu/en/projects/Eurotech-x-HKTE-Hackathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold text-brand-teal hover:underline">
          Read the story behind the project
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Business Concept & Hong Kong Fit -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-brand-beige/25 border-t border-brand-navy/5 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-peach bg-brand-peach/10 px-3 py-1 rounded">
            The Market Opportunity
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
            Strategic Fit: Hong Kong & Global Expansion
          </h2>
          <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Mental health is a critical concern in high-density markets like Hong Kong. Figures compiled by the Legislative Council Research Office put the share of people with a mental disorder at <strong>13% of working adults, 24% of youth and 12.5% of the elderly</strong>, with depression, bipolar disorder and anxiety the most common. Most cases are recognised late, when treatment is long and expensive.
          </p>
          <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Hong Kong is the ideal launchpad due to two unique advantages:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-navy/80">
              <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-brand-teal/15 text-brand-teal flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>Hybrid Insurance System:</strong> The split between private and government-funded care rewards insurers who manage chronic risks early.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-navy/80">
              <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-brand-teal/15 text-brand-teal flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5 font-bold">✓</span>
              <span><strong>East-Meets-West Digital Intersection:</strong> Access to both Western (YouTube, Instagram, Spotify) and Eastern ecosystems enables training models for seamless future expansion into China.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-3xl border border-brand-navy/15 shadow-sm space-y-6 relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-24 h-24 bg-brand-teal/5 rounded-full blur-xl pointer-events-none"></div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-brand-navy border-b border-brand-navy/5 pb-3">How the Data Flows</h3>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-brand-navy/5 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-brand-navy text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">01</div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm">Data Export by the User</h4>
                <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 mt-1">Users download their own data package from YouTube, Instagram or TikTok, a right every platform grants under privacy law (GDPR and equivalents).</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-brand-teal/10 text-brand-teal flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">02</div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm">Anonymous Upload & Digital Biomarkers</h4>
                <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 mt-1">Videos and photos are removed in the browser before upload. Under an anonymous LDiHK-ID we extract only timing signals: daily volume, fragmentation and late-night use. No names, handles or messages are stored.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-brand-peach/10 text-brand-peach flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs shrink-0 mt-0.5">03</div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-sm">Risk Signal & Prevention</h4>
                <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 mt-1">The user sees their own patterns compared with people of the same age and sex. With consent, insurers use the risk signal for rewards and early, low-threshold support offers.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Science: mathematical groundwork -->
  <section id="science" class="py-20 bg-white text-left border-t border-brand-navy/5">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-14 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
          The Science Behind the Score
        </h2>
        <p class="text-brand-navy/70 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-base leading-relaxed">
          A neural network that links social media use to medical conditions needs a lot of training data. Partnering insurers provide it in Phase 1. Until then, a mathematical model built from independent, peer-reviewed studies serves as the starting point.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-brand-beige/30 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Built on Published Evidence</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/70 leading-relaxed">
            We combined findings of peer-reviewed studies on social media use and depression (e.g. Kelly et al. 2018, Lin et al. 2016, Primack et al. 2017, Riehm et al. 2019 and a dose-response meta-analysis by Liu et al. 2022), including their adjusted odds ratios, into one database and fit an initial linear model to them. It validates the pipeline and scoring logic and is the basis for a machine-learning model as the dataset grows.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-brand-beige/30 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Three Models by Age</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/70 leading-relaxed">
            Digital stressors affect age groups very differently, so one model would not suffice. We use separate models for adolescents, young adults and older adults, with sex as a further baseline. It adds complexity in the backend but delivers more reliable results, a trade-off we consider essential for the standards of HealthTech.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-brand-beige/30 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Focused on Depression First</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/70 leading-relaxed">
            We deliberately start with depression: the most prevalent and best-studied mental health disorder. It offers the highest achievable accuracy and the largest potential impact, for public health and for insurers' costs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Digital Biomarkers Today</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-brand-navy/80">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-teal font-bold">&bull;</span><span><strong>Daily volume:</strong> watch and usage time per day across the uploaded platforms.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-teal font-bold">&bull;</span><span><strong>Fragmentation:</strong> how many hours of the day are interrupted by usage.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-teal font-bold">&bull;</span><span><strong>Late-night use:</strong> activity between 23:00 and 05:00 that disrupts the circadian rhythm.</span></li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-teal font-bold">&bull;</span><span><strong>Demographic baselines:</strong> age range and sex, because usage and risk differ strongly between groups.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">All of them are tracked over time, to recognise personal patterns and recent changes rather than single days.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Coming Next</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-brand-navy/80 leading-relaxed">
            The format and content of what is consumed (short-form video or public forums, Instagram hashtags), comments and more markers, plus validation against real outcomes once partner data is available. A first validation of the pipeline and scoring logic was done with a sample group of peers; large-scale validation still needs more data.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stakeholder Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white text-left">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-16 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
          The Stakeholder Ecosystem
        </h2>
        <p class="text-brand-navy/70 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-base">
          Creating shared value for users, private insurers, healthcare experts, and society.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <!-- Insurers -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow group text-left">
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-brand-navy/5 text-brand-navy flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Insurance Providers</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              Gain competitive advantages in risk underwriting, lower long-term claims liabilities, and foster direct customer engagement through wellness incentive loops.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Users -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow group text-left">
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-brand-teal/10 text-brand-teal flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 01-8 0m8 2a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Policyholders / Users</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              See their own digital habits for free, compared with people like them. Optionally share them with their insurer for premium offsets or vouchers and early, low-threshold support. They can delete everything at any time.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Clinicians -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow group text-left">
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-brand-peach/10 text-brand-peach flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19.428 15.428a2 2 0 00-1.022-.547l-2.387-.477a6 6 0 00-3.86.517l-.318.158a6 6 0 01-3.86.517L6.05 15.21a2 2 0 00-1.806.547M8 4h8l-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 00.586 1.414l5 5c1.26 1.26.367 3.414-1.415 3.414H4.828c-1.782 0-2.674-2.154-1.414-3.414l5-5A2 2 0 009 10.172V5L8 4z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">Healthcare Experts</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              With the user's consent, receive an early risk signal and the behavioural trend behind it, so preventive conversations can start sooner.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Society -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-brand-navy/10 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between hover:shadow-md transition-shadow group text-left">
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-brand-beige text-brand-navy/80 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm6 3a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zM7 10a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">The Public & Society</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              Alleviates systemic pressure on public mental health systems, leading to a healthier, happier, and more productive workforce.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Business Roadmap Section -->
  <section id="roadmap" class="py-20 bg-brand-beige/20 border-t border-b border-brand-navy/5 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-16 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
          Venture Deployment Roadmap
        </h2>
        <p class="text-brand-navy/70 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-base">
          The three-phase roadmap we pitched at the hackathon for bringing preventive mental wellness insurance to life.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-8 relative before:absolute before:inset-0 before:left-4 sm:before:left-1/2 before:w-0.5 before:bg-brand-navy/10 before:pointer-events-none">

        <!-- Phase 1 -->
        <div class="relative flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:justify-between group">
          <div class="absolute left-4 sm:left-1/2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-brand-teal border-4 border-white -translate-x-1.5 mt-2 shadow-sm z-10 transition-colors group-hover:bg-brand-peach"></div>

          <div class="w-full sm:w-[45%] pl-10 sm:pl-0 sm:text-right space-y-2">
            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-bold bg-brand-teal/10 text-brand-teal uppercase tracking-wide">
              Phase 1: Ingestion & Training (Years 1-2)
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy">Model Integration & Health Record Pairing</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              Partner insurers incentivise policyholders to share their data exports. Paired with anonymised claims records, they form the training data for a machine-learning model that replaces the study-based starting model, beginning with depression and later anxiety and stress.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden sm:block w-[45%]"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Phase 2 -->
        <div class="relative flex flex-col sm:flex-row-reverse items-start sm:justify-between group">
          <div class="absolute left-4 sm:left-1/2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-brand-teal border-4 border-white -translate-x-1.5 mt-2 shadow-sm z-10 transition-colors group-hover:bg-brand-peach"></div>

          <div class="w-full sm:w-[45%] pl-10 sm:pl-0 space-y-2">
            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-bold bg-brand-teal/10 text-brand-teal uppercase tracking-wide">
              Phase 2: Preventative Intervention
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy">Voucher Incentives & Early Treatments</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              Using the early-warning models, insurance providers identify high-risk usage patterns in real-time. Insurers offer tailored vouchers and preventative clinical treatments, resolving wellness issues before they become severe, significantly lowering treatment liabilities.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden sm:block w-[45%]"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Phase 3 -->
        <div class="relative flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:justify-between group">
          <div class="absolute left-4 sm:left-1/2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-brand-teal border-4 border-white -translate-x-1.5 mt-2 shadow-sm z-10 transition-colors group-hover:bg-brand-peach"></div>

          <div class="w-full sm:w-[45%] pl-10 sm:pl-0 sm:text-right space-y-2">
            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-bold bg-brand-teal/10 text-brand-teal uppercase tracking-wide">
              Phase 3: Smart Underwriting
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy">Dynamic Underwriting & Applicant Rewards</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-brand-navy/60 leading-relaxed">
              We transition to underwriting. New applicants who voluntarily verify their digital footprints receive custom insurance plans and discounts for displaying low-risk habits, creating a substantial competitive advantage for partner insurers.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden sm:block w-[45%]"></div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MVP Details Section -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-white text-left">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-teal bg-brand-teal/10 px-3 py-1 rounded">
            What You Can Try Today
          </span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
            The Working Prototype
          </h2>
          <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            The console is a working prototype, not a trained clinical model. It runs the complete data pipeline end to end: upload your own export, get an anonymous LDiHK-ID, and explore your habits within minutes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-brand-navy/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Your history (YouTube, Instagram, TikTok) appears as a timeline, a 24-hour heatmap and a day-by-day breakdown. The population benchmark compares you with people of your age range and sex: about 1,500 synthetic profiles calibrated on the cited studies, plus real users as they join. The health tab shows the study-based risk indicator, for self-reflection, not as a diagnosis.
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-t border-brand-navy/10 pt-6">
            <div>
              <span class="text-2xl font-black text-brand-teal block">3</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold text-brand-navy/60">Platforms Imported</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <span class="text-2xl font-black text-brand-peach block">0</span>
              <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold text-brand-navy/60">Names or Handles Stored</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-brand-beige/40 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-brand-navy/10 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-extrabold text-brand-navy text-lg">What the console measures:</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-xs">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-brand-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold">1</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-brand-navy">Screen Volume Index:</strong>
                <span class="block text-brand-navy/70 mt-0.5">Estimated watch time per day across the uploaded platforms. Each additional hour of social media use is associated with higher depression risk in adolescents (Liu et al. 2022).</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-brand-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold">2</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-brand-navy">Circadian Disruption Index:</strong>
                <span class="block text-brand-navy/70 mt-0.5">Usage between 23:00 and 05:00, which delays sleep; poor sleep is one of the pathways between heavy social media use and depressive symptoms (Kelly et al. 2018).</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-brand-navy/10 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 font-bold">3</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-brand-navy">Task Fragmentation Index:</strong>
                <span class="block text-brand-navy/70 mt-0.5">How many hours of the day are interrupted by usage: frequent checking throughout the day rather than one block.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- General Info & Support Footer-Card -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-brand-beige border-t border-brand-navy/10 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute right-0 bottom-0 w-64 h-64 bg-brand-peach/10 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center relative z-10 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy tracking-tight">
        Questions or Feedback?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-brand-navy/70 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        LDiHK is a hackathon prototype. If you have questions about the project or the model, found a bug or have an idea for the console, write to us or use the feedback form.
      </p>

      <div class="inline-flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="mailto:contact@LDiHK.xyz"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-navy text-white font-bold text-sm hover:bg-brand-navy/95 transition-all shadow-md shadow-brand-navy/10 hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5 duration-150"
          id="main-contact-email"
        >
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-brand-peach" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
